{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\user\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -LiteralPath 'C:\\\\Projects\\\\Agent_Workspace\\\\HG-KSEOS\\\\var\\\\swof-construction-002-w2-repair-001\\\\specs\\\\R3_WO-SWOF-W2-R007_SPEC.md' -Raw\"","aggregated_output":"# R3 WO-SWOF-W2-R007 — exact §15.5 basis bytes, current HumanGateDecision/authority lineage, canonical signed sets\n\nrepair_id: SWOF-W2-CLOSURE-R3\nbase: b8e62b96463273e3475ff52a7a4a87831816927a   (the R2 candidate)\norigin: two new external FAIL_CHALLENGE reports (A found 1 blocker, B found 4). All four were INDEPENDENTLY\n        REPRODUCED by deterministic recomputation from the frozen PI06 text before any mutation —\n        evidence/R3_BASELINE_ADJUDICATION.json. Report A under-reported; B is correct.\n\n## Verified defects at the frozen base\n\n### A. approval_basis_hash byte recipe is NOT the frozen §15.5 formula\nPI06 §15.5 is DIRECT byte concatenation with exactly ONE newline inside the domain frame:\n    SHA256(b\"SWOF-D03-APPROVAL-BASIS-V1\\n\" || decision_basis_hash || effect_digest ||\n           generation_bundle_digest || rollback_digest || consumer_audience_hash || if06b_version)\nThe shipped `approval_basis_hash` uses `\"\\n\".join((...))` over the six fields, adding FIVE extra\ninter-field newline bytes (its own docstring documents this). Independent recomputation:\n  frozen formula   -> 2a868198e40141f4ccfdcf5767fcb4f5950a3c241fc04b32de7d173cb79e6992\n  shipped recipe   -> b7965468fb4b11f51c44342d8aefe92c2120a8eb5ed648678f3c09d85eb91080\nThey differ. The shipped test constructs its expected value with the SAME newline recipe, so maker test\nand maker implementation agree while both contradict the frozen source.\n\n### B. request→HumanGateDecision→ApprovalToken authority/decision lineage is under-bound\n`required_authority` exists only as an `ApprovalRequest` dataclass field (humangate.py:359); it is\nNEVER consumed by the verifier and appears 0 times in rights.py. `HumanGateDecision` does not exist in\nthe module at all. `request.decision_basis_hash` is a caller-supplied string consumed as-is. So a\nwell-signed token with an insufficient/stale authority class, or one bound to a decision that was never\nresolved, has no first-fail path: signature validity is being used as a proxy for canonical authority.\n\n### C. signed `resource`/`scope` sets are not canonicalized\nPI06 §16.2: `scope` is a set (unique + bytewise UTF-8 lexical sort); `resource` is a set (unique +\ncanonical resource-ID lexical sort); signed-object arrays MUST carry\n`x-swof-collection-semantics: set|sequence` and a missing annotation is a SCHEMA ERROR.\nAt the base: the schema has 2 array properties and 0 annotations; `canonical_payload_bytes` does not sort\nthem; JCS of two permutations of the SAME semantic set differ. So one semantic approval subject has more\nthan one accepted canonical signed byte representation.\n\n### D. final evidence transport is internally inconsistent (evidence phase, not product cone)\nIn the committed evidence blob: the Return Pack still says `w2_evidence_commit_sha: null`,\n`publication.remote_push: NOT_ATTEMPTED`, `pr_number: null`, branch\n`wo/swof-w2-security-effect-assurance` — while its own claim ceiling includes\n`NEW_EVIDENCE_COMMIT_PUBLISHED`; the dossier at the final path is still titled \"R1\" with\n`repair_id: SWOF-W2-CLOSURE-R1`; and the External Readset is absent from the evidence commit (0\noccurrences) although the publication receipt claims it is in the commit.\n\n## Required product implementation (smallest existing-seam change; NO new authority or crypto subsystem)\n\n### A. Exact basis bytes\nReplace the materialization with the frozen direct concatenation — NO separator bytes between the six\nfields, only the single newline already inside APPROVAL_BASIS_FRAME. Add a golden vector whose expected\ndigest is a LITERAL source-derived constant (`2a868198e40141f4ccfdcf5767fcb4f5950a3c241fc04b32de7d173cb79e6992`)\nand which does NOT call `approval_basis_hash` to build its expected value. The old\n`b7965468...` value must be asserted UNEQUAL / rejected.\n\n### B. Current authority + HumanGateDecision lineage (typed, owner-injected — do not invent an authority system)\nAdd the smallest typed seam that lets an owner supply canonical authority/decision facts:\n1. a `HumanGateDecision` value object carrying at least: `decision_id`, `request_id`, `approver`,\n   `authority_class`, `authn_assurance_class`, `executable_state` (e.g. APPROVE), `revoked`,\n   `superseded`, and the `ApprovalDecisionBasisV1` basis fields;\n2. a `decision_resolver` on `VerificationContext` (injected callable/registry) that resolves a\n   `decision_id` to the current canonical decision, and an `authority_policy` seam that decides whether a\n   decision's authority satisfies the request's `required_authority`.\nThe verifier must then establish, in first-fail order, on a gated path:\n   - request `required_authority` is present/canonical, else deny;\n   - a current decision resolves `decision_id`, else deny (`DENY_DECISION_UNRESOLVED`);\n   - `decision.request_id == request.request_id`, else deny (`DENY_DECISION_REQUEST_MISMATCH`);\n   - `decision.decision_id == token.decision_id`, else deny (`DENY_DECISION_TOKEN_MISMATCH`);\n   - decision is executable APPROVE and not revoked/superseded/stale, else deny;\n   - `authority_policy(decision.authority_class, request.required_authority)` holds, else deny\n     (`DENY_INSUFFICIENT_AUTHORITY`). Do NOT invent an HA ordering: if the policy seam is absent the check\n     FAILS CLOSED with a typed denial, and if the project has no canonical owner able to define that\n     policy within this cone, emit `TEMP_CLOSED_AUTHORITY_RESOLUTION` with the exact missing owner\n     interface rather than guessing a ranking;\n   - decision authn meets the request floor, else deny;\n   - `decision_basis_hash` is INDEPENDENTLY reconstructed as `SHA256(JCS(ApprovalDecisionBasisV1))` from\n     the resolved decision basis and compared to the request's value, else deny\n     (`DENY_DECISION_BASIS_MISMATCH`);\n   - only then recompute the token's `approval_basis_hash` (now via the exact §15.5 bytes).\nA gated path with no resolvable decision must FAIL CLOSED. Update the existing fixtures so the positive\ncontrols inject a canonical current decision + sufficient authority.\n\n### C. Canonical signed sets\n- Normalize at the canonical representation boundary BEFORE JCS: `resource` sorted by canonical\n  resource-ID lexical order; `scope` sorted bytewise UTF-8 lexical order; both de-duplicated.\n- Reject duplicate or malformed atoms fail-closed rather than silently accepting a second byte form.\n- Add `\"x-swof-collection-semantics\": \"set\"` to the `resource` and `scope` array properties in\n  `schemas/security/approval_token.schema.json`, and assert the annotation is present and equals \"set\".\n- One semantic set must yield exactly ONE canonical signed byte representation (permutation-invariant).\n\n## Required focused tests (source-derived expected values; do not call the helper under test)\n    A1 literal golden vector -> 2a868198e40141f4ccfdcf5767fcb4f5950a3c241fc04b32de7d173cb79e6992\n    A2 the old newline recipe -> UNEQUAL / denied\n    A3 otherwise-valid token with wrong basis -> DENY_APPROVAL_BASIS\n    B1 insufficient authority for the requirement -> DENY_INSUFFICIENT_AUTHORITY\n    B2 unknown authority_class -> deny\n    B3 stale/revoked/superseded decision or authority -> deny\n    B4 nonexistent decision_id -> DENY_DECISION_UNRESOLVED\n    B5 decision bound to another request -> DENY_DECISION_REQUEST_MISMATCH\n    B6 decision_id not matching the token -> DENY_DECISION_TOKEN_MISMATCH\n    B7 caller decision_basis_hash not matching recomputed JCS basis -> DENY_DECISION_BASIS_MISMATCH\n    B8 canonical current decision + sufficient authority -> PASS (positive control)\n    C1 resource permutation A/B -> IDENTICAL canonical payload bytes\n    C2 scope permutation A/B -> IDENTICAL canonical payload bytes\n    C3 framed digest invariant under semantic set permutation\n    C4 duplicate resource/scope atom -> deny\n    C5 malformed atom -> deny\n    C6 schema resource annotation == \"set\"\n    C7 schema scope annotation == \"set\"\n    + all prior invariants retained (P3 floor, RUIN/UNKNOWN_RUIN, unknown-operation safe-stop,\n      JCS/domain-frame/Ed25519, lineage/audience/generations, T3 checker, approver != actor)\n\n## Constraints\n- write-set: `src/security/humangate.py`, `schemas/security/approval_token.schema.json`,\n  `src/security/tests/test_humangate_currentness.py`, `src/security/tests/test_rights.py`;\n  `src/security/rights.py` ONLY if the gate predicate must change to carry the authority edge.\n- no second HumanGate/router/authority system; extend the existing seam.\n- no new crypto; keep RFC 8785 JCS + domain frame + real Ed25519.\n- every change neutral-or-stricter; do not weaken any existing refusal.\n- do not edit tests to match code where the frozen source says otherwise.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
