ch new effect needs a new token/decision | prefill context may reduce typing but MUST NOT preselect approval |\n| T3 | high-salience view; consequences/irreversibility/checker status above fold | batch approval forbidden | short TTL; explicit affirm action; deny/cancel equally accessible |\n\n**Progressive disclosure law:** critical fields—operation, target, scope, data/rights impact, downside, irreversibility, rollback, permission class, T2/T3 status, required checker/coapprovers, expiry—cannot be hidden behind optional expansion. Localization may change wording, never semantics. Accessibility support MUST preserve the same fields in machine-readable accessibility tree.\n\n## 14.5 ApprovalView provenance\n\nThe runtime MUST hash the exact canonical `ApprovalDecisionBasisV1` used to render the view and record `view_render_receipt` with locale, accessibility mode, presentation schema version and field-presence bitset. UI click/chat reply/provider OAuth remains an input event only; `HumanGateDecision` is produced only after canonical mapping and authority/authn validation.\n\n## 14.R｜Retained r1 details under r2 closure\n\n`HUMAN_GATE_POLICY_SPEC` materializes deterministic rule IDs rather than placeholder prose:\n\n```yaml\nHumanGatePolicy:\n  action_class: operation_class\n  effect_risk_tier: LOW | MEDIUM | HIGH | CRITICAL | RUIN | UNKNOWN_RUIN\n  subject_risk_class: risk_class_ref\n  permission_class: P0 | P1 | P2 | P3 | P4 | P5\n  requirement_rule_id: HG-RULE-*\n  required_human_authority: authority_requirement\n  required_coapprovals: [authority_requirement]\n  required_authn_assurance: AAC1 | AAC2 | AAC3\n  max_reauth_age: duration_policy\n  decision_scope: scope_contract\n  purpose_binding: purpose_ref\n  evidence_shown_to_approver: evidence_projection_contract\n  approval_requirement_schema: ApprovalRequirementSchemaRef\n  human_gate_decision_schema: HumanGateDecisionSchemaRef\n  approval_token_schema: ApprovalTokenSchemaRef\n  expiry: expiry_policy\n  trusted