{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_61","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\user\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command '$f='\"'C:\\\\Projects\\\\Agent_Workspace\\\\知識庫\\\\實作相關DOC\\\\Fabric vNext\\\\Semantic World OS Fabric\\\\SWOF-F_SWOF-GENIE_All-IW_Pre-Dev_Multi-Packages\\\\PI-PKG\\\\DOC\\\\PI-PKG-06_DOC\\\\SWOF-F_SWOF-GENIE_All-IW_PI-PKG-06_DOC-03_2026-09-10_r2_FULL_REPAIR.md'; \"'$lines = Get-Content -LiteralPath $f; $lines[1120..1200] -join \"`n\"'","aggregated_output":"# 16｜Token Admission Invariants / Time / Integrity / Exact Binding\n\n## 16.0 Deterministic token admission invariants\n\n| ID | Condition | First-fail result |\n|---|---|---|\n| TOK-INV-001 | P3/P4/P5 without valid exact Human token | `DENY_P3_TOKEN_REQUIRED` |\n| TOK-INV-002 | subject/hash/op/target/resource/purpose/scope/data/environment mismatch | `DENY_EXACT_BINDING` |\n| TOK-INV-003 | commit time outside issuance/expiry window | `DENY_TOKEN_TIME` |\n| TOK-INV-004 | token_state != ACTIVE | `DENY_TOKEN_STATE` |\n| TOK-INV-005 | nonce/idempotency already consumed/reserved incompatibly | `DENY_REPLAY` |\n| TOK-INV-006 | rights/security/provider/authn/key/ruin generation stale | `DENY_STALE_GENERATION` |\n| TOK-INV-007 | required rollback ref unresolved | `DENY_NO_ROLLBACK` |\n| TOK-INV-008 | model/tool/provider asserts Human authority | `DENY_FALSE_AUTHORITY` |\n| TOK-INV-009 | effect = RUIN or UNKNOWN_RUIN | `HARD_VETO` / `SAFE_STOP` |\n| TOK-INV-010 | canonicalization/signature/key trust fails | `DENY_TOKEN_INTEGRITY` |\n| TOK-INV-011 | consumer audience mismatch | `DENY_AUDIENCE_MISMATCH` |\n| TOK-INV-012 | UI/protocol approve event without canonical decision/token | `DENY_FALSE_AUTHORITY` |\n| TOK-INV-013 | approver authn assurance/freshness insufficient | `DENY_AUTHN` |\n| TOK-INV-014 | AutonomyTier=T3 without current independent checker evidence | `DENY_T3_CHECKER` |\n\n\n\n## 16.1A TOKEN_TIME_VALIDITY_SPEC\n\n- `issued_at`, `reauthenticated_at`, `expires_at` are RFC3339 UTC `Z`.\n- Token admission requires `issued_at <= commit_time < expires_at`; equality at expiry is invalid.\n- Clock skew tolerance is a **health tolerance for comparing sources**, never an extension of token TTL.\n- If wall-clock uncertainty or disagreement could flip a validity decision, result is `SAFE_STOP`; no “grace approval”.\n- Contextual expiry may occur earlier than absolute expiry when any bound generation, authority, audience, effect digest or provider generation changes.\n- T3 and P4/P5 policies MAY impose shorter TTL than T2/P3; they MUST NOT impose a longer TTL than parent/domain maximum.\n\n## 16.1 SWOF-HG-INTEGRITY-001 canonical serialization\n\nCanonical token integrity is frozen as a standards-composed profile:\n\n1. Payload is UTF-8 JSON.\n2. Canonical bytes are RFC 8785 JCS over `ApprovalToken` **excluding `signature`**.\n3. JCS does not Unicode-normalize strings; producers MUST preserve exact JSON string scalar sequence. Protocol identifiers are restricted to canonical ASCII where their registry allows.\n4. Domain framing bytes are `bytes(\"SWOF:PI-PKG-06:DOC-03:APPROVAL-TOKEN:V1\\\\0\") || JCS(payload_without_signature)`.\n5. Signature algorithm is Ed25519; signature is exactly 64 raw bytes encoded Base64url without `=`.\n6. `key_id` is an opaque, case-sensitive ASCII identifier; `key_generation` is unsigned integer. Verifier resolves both from the canonical key registry.\n7. SHA-256 digests are lowercase 64-hex.\n8. Time is RFC3339 UTC; trusted-clock uncertainty beyond configured skew fails closed.\n\n## 16.2 Array semantics registry\n\n| Field | Semantics | Canonicalization |\n|---|---|---|\n| scope | set | unique; bytewise UTF-8 lexical sort of canonical atoms |\n| resource when multiple | set | unique; canonical resource ID lexical sort |\n| required_coapprovals | set | unique authority refs; lexical sort |\n| reason_codes | set | unique registered codes; lexical sort |\n| changed_basis_refs | set | unique canonical refs; lexical sort |\n| evidence_summary_ref | set unless owner marks sequence | sort canonical refs |\n| ordered workflow steps inside referenced objects | sequence | preserve owner order; never sort |\n\nSchema annotations MUST state `x-swof-collection-semantics: set|sequence`. Missing annotation on an array in a signed object is a schema error.\n\n## 16.3 TOKEN_ENVELOPE_SBB_DECISION\n\n| Option | Reuse value | Fit / no-fit | Disposition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| JOSE/JWS | mature envelope, key IDs, broad libraries; RFC 9864 now provides fully-specified `Ed25519` identifier | adds protected-header/base64 payload envelope and a second canonical representation; SWOF needs one human-readable JSON object whose exact bytes are approval evidence | `SELECTED_FALLBACK_INTEROP_ADAPTER`; not canonical token bytes |\n| COSE/CBOR | compact, mature constrained-device ecosystem | canonical CBOR would create a second binary canonical form and migration burden for ApprovalView/evidence tooling | `SELECTED_FALLBACK_PHYSICAL_INTEROP`; not canonical source token |\n| RFC8785 JCS + Ed25519 framed signature | reuses standardized canonical JSON + standardized signature primitive; minimal profile | requires SWOF profile definition but no custom crypto primitive | `SELECTED_PRIMARY_PROTOCOL` |\n\nThe choice is not “home-grown cryptography”: only composition/framing is SWOF-specific. Crypto primitive, canonical JSON and hashing are standard. Future replacement requires parity on exact binding, deterministic bytes, anti-replay, key generations, cross-language vectors and human-readable evidence.\n\n## 16.4 Golden vectors — TEST ONLY\n\nTest seed: `000102030405060708090a0b0c0d0e0f101112131415161718191a1b1c1d1e1f`; public key Base64url: `A6EHv_POEL4dcN0Y50vAmWfk1jCbpQ1fHdyGZBJVMbg`. This key is **fixture-only** and MUST never appear in runtime trust stores.\n\n| Vector | Framed SHA-256 | Ed25519 signature Base64url |\n|---|---|---|\n| GV-001 | `9e3cd0001b0de96e1a9bee9e8dda0de7876e67aa917298ddd8c4a4e38d0b3022` | `IDRL4xWaMA84wckiV6AT8ocavkMfz3Wd2d_nnsnK1R692Os8HL7v1YLuAurDrv_q7gbHN1Vsv7_oR8k7nJjgBg` |\n| GV-002 | `2f29f47c05589bd64058abb8e1aa817dd2a4e8a5e5bf5eda86df8ae88b9e28a2` | `swSfLRliojZLXQjQeSTXlDfyOvPGypKUDC_0KdE4k8xZ72bcSaYD5FQmtk2DuhrPtuFqydZ1-zINl-7u-g-DBw` |\n| GV-003 | `18591eebe2486feef79c33e76f2ed060bfe0e8cdb960e5f21a0c2aa7807a311a` | `jXjU7U4-zrfjJ0TsZy5sz6LMSNoPrqw7ph95QhcDJeghNeIk-lhYx0D0_sQpopbvEuBi_pllHEmA9bq2DnSpDQ` |\n\nPre-Dev MUST reproduce these vectors independently in at least three implementation languages before parity acceptance; expected-evidence targets do not equal executed evidence.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
